00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:07.430 align:start position:0%
eu finance ministers meeting in brussels  will prepare the greek presidency's  monday to finalize negotiations with the  european parliament on the proposal for  a single resolution mechanism to rescue  failing banks this is one of the key  elements of the banking union which aims  to enable in-depth restructuring of  banks undergoing serious financial  problems the greek presidency will  pursue its efforts to iron out  differences with the european parliament  in order to reach a final agreement  before the end of the current  parliamentary term the council will also  be called on to adopt a proposal to  strengthen rules on taxing savings  income derived from interest payments  the new rules will require paying agents  to report interest income received by  taxpayers resident in other eu member  states member states must automatically  exchange information that will enable  interest payments made in one country to  residents of another to be taxed in  accordance with the laws of the state of  tax residents the new directive includes  all types of savings income and products  and requires the collaboration of tax  authorities in establishing the identity  of beneficial owners ministers will also  have an exchange of views on the  economic elements of the eu 2030 energy  and climate framework
 

